<h2>Why the guest sounds quieter</h2>
<p>The host talks into their own microphone, in a studio they know. The guest brings a different microphone, sits in a different room, and sometimes joins over a remote call. So each voice enters the episode at its own level.</p>
<p>Editing makes sure the episode as a whole plays at a sensible level, but the gap between the two people talking in it usually stays. At home it's a little annoying. In a car, with road noise, it means your hand is on the knob the whole time.</p>

<h2>What the app does</h2>
<p>LevelCast listens to the episode as it plays and fixes the gap as it goes, so the quiet voice comes up and the loud one comes down a little. All of this happens on the phone. The producer's file stays as it is, and no audio gets sent anywhere for levelling.</p>

