<p>There are three strengths. <strong>Normal</strong> is the lighter touch. <strong>Strong</strong> closes bigger gaps and suits a noisy car, and <strong>Off</strong> plays the episode exactly as it arrived. You can <a href="{{ collections.byKey.listen[lang] }}">hear the difference in the demo</a>.</p>

<h2>Where the episodes come from</h2>
<p>Podcasts are published in an open feed, and the audio itself sits on the producer's server. The app finds shows in Apple's podcast directory, and you can also paste in a feed address or an episode link by hand. The episode plays straight from the producer's server, and the download is counted there.</p>

<h2>Everything inside</h2>
<ul class="checks">
  <li><strong>Speaker levelling</strong> at normal or strong, and you can set a different strength for each show.</li>
  <li><strong>Intro skip.</strong> The app spots where the music ends and the conversation starts, and offers to jump there.</li>
  <li><strong>Pace matching.</strong> Whoever talks slowly is sped up a little, and whoever rushes is slowed down.</li>
  <li><strong>Playback speed</strong> from <span dir="ltr">0.5×</span> to <span dir="ltr">3×</span>.</li>
  <li><strong>Capture a moment.</strong> Hold the back button on your steering wheel, or tap the button in the player, to save what was just said along with its transcript. Moments wait in your library, and you send them once you've stopped.</li>
  <li><strong>Live transcript</strong> that scrolls like song lyrics, <strong>search inside the episode</strong>, and <strong>key points</strong> built from sentences actually said in it. Transcription uses iOS speech recognition, on devices that support the episode's language.</li>
  <li><strong>The links from the episode notes</strong>, all in one place.</li>
  <li><strong>A short automatic rewind</strong> after an interruption, so the end of the sentence doesn't slip past you.</li>
  <li><strong>Downloads</strong> by hand, automatically or ahead of time, and a background refresh that tells you when a new episode is out.</li>
  <li><strong>Sleep timer</strong> that lowers the sound gradually at the end, instead of cutting a sentence in half.</li>
</ul>

