<h2>Privacy</h2>
<p>There's no account and no sign-up. Your library, queue, moments and settings are kept only on your phone. The app contacts Apple when you search for a show, and the producer's server to fetch the feed and the audio. Transcription runs on the phone too. On a device that can't recognise speech locally in the episode's language, transcription isn't available, and the audio isn't sent anywhere. All the details are in the <a href="{{ collections.byKey.privacy[lang] }}">privacy policy</a>.</p>

<h2>Which devices</h2>
<p>You need an iPhone with iOS 17 or later. The interface is in Hebrew and English.</p>
